    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nAvalon is a superbly positioned deceptively large three-bedroom detached residence with garage and separate self-contained granny flat, set on a unassumingly large south-facing site. While the property requires extensive refurbishment and modernisation throughout, it offers exceptional potential for discerning purchasers seeking to create a bespoke family home or investment opportunity.\n\nThe property is being offered for sale together with the adjoining residence, Hollymount (two separate sales), presenting a rare and highly attractive redevelopment prospect in one of Cork's most sought-after residential locations.\n\nIdeally situated on Hartlands Avenue, directly opposite The Lough Nature Reserve, the location is truly second to none. Rarely does a development opportunity arise to acquire a property in such a prime setting, with immediate access to a wealth of amenities including University College Cork (UCC), Bons Secours Hospital, Cork University Hospital (CUH), Cork city centre, and the extensive south ring road network. \n\nThis is a unique opportunity that should not be missed."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nPorch - 1.94m x 0.87m\nStep in porch with an original terrazzo floor.\n\nEntrance Hall - 3.81, x 1.96m\nFeaturing an original terrazzo floor, picture rails and under stairs storage.\n\nLiving Room - 4.73m x 3.77m + 2.36m x 1.04m\nWell-proportioned and bright reception room with a large bay window, original tiled fireplace and original picture rails. There is built-in shelving within the alcoves.\n\nDining Room - 5.98m x 3.84m\nLarge bright room to the rear of the property enjoying a sunny south facing aspect and an original fireplace with timber mantal and cast iron & tile insert. Original picture rails. There is direct access to the kitchen.\n\nKitchen - 4.05m x 1.96m\nThere is an original terrazzo floor. Door leading to the back hall that leads to the south facing rear garden.\n\nBack Hall - 1.68m x 0.92m\nTiled floor and door leading to the garden.\n\nGarage - 11.20m x 3.10m\nIdeal for conversion or as a storage area.\n\nBedroom 1 - 4.25m x 4.22m + 2.34m x 1.04m\nLarge bright double bedroom with a bay window and an original fireplace with a timber mantal and tiled insert. Original picture rails.\n\nBedroom 2 - 4.88m x 3.39m\nSpacious double bedroom to the rear with an original fireplace with timber mantal and tiled insert. There are original picture rails, built-in closet and hotpress store.\n\nBedroom 3 - 2.49m x 2.27m\nBright single bedroom to the front. Original picture rails.\n\nFirst Floor Landing - \nStairs to a floored attic space.\n\nGRANNY FLAT - \n\n\nEntrance Hall - 4.41m x 0.92m\nWalk-in hotpress / storage closet.\n\nLiving Room - 3.72m x 3.36m\nFeaturing an open fireplace with timber mantal with cast iron insert. Shelved alcove.\n\nKitchenet - 2.72m x 1.29m\nPlumbed for sink unit.\n\nBedroom - 4.76m x 3.11m\nSpacious double bedroom with shower unit to one side.\n\nWC - 1.28m x 0.89m\nTwo-piece suite.\n\n"
      },
